{"tool_name":"gbc","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"gbc","home":"https://pmglab.top/gbc","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"Parallel toolkit based on highly addressable byte-encoding blocks for extremely large-scale genotypes of species.","addition_date":"2023-11-10T13:38:19.090710Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:31:56.312626Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:gbc","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"limiaoxin@mail.sysu.edu.cn","name":"Miaoxin Li","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4733-0109","typeEntity":"Person"}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"http://pmglab.top/gbc/api-docs/"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://pmglab.top/gbc/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Linkage disequilibrium calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0488"},{"term":"Splitting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3359"}]}],"name":"GBC","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-023-02906-z","metadata":{"abstract":"Whole-genome sequencing projects of millions of subjects contain enormous genotypes, entailing a huge memory burden and time for computation. Here, we present GBC, a toolkit for rapidly compressing large-scale genotypes into highly addressable byte-encoding blocks under an optimized parallel framework. We demonstrate that GBC is up to 1000 times faster than state-of-the-art methods to access and manage compressed large-scale genotypes while maintaining a competitive compression ratio. We also showed that conventional analysis would be substantially sped up if built on GBC to access genotypes of a large population. GBC\u2019s data structure and algorithms are valuable for acce